1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,688
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,688 --> 00:00:04,460
OTTO: Oh no! The till won't balance!

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,952
IVY: The sheet and the money don't match.

4
00:00:08,352 --> 00:00:11,821
Today's case: the till that won't balance.

5
00:00:12,121 --> 00:00:16,161
Regroup means swapping ten ones for one ten.

6
00:00:16,561 --> 00:00:21,363
Like ten one-dollar coins for a ten-dollar note.

7
00:00:21,963 --> 00:00:24,980
The till started with 38 dollars.

8
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:29,819
Then the kiosk sold 27 dollars of icy poles.

9
00:00:30,219 --> 00:00:34,933
OTTO: Easy! Eight plus seven is fifteen. I'll write five.

10
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:39,229
OTTO: Three plus two is five. So, 55 dollars!

11
00:00:39,629 --> 00:00:42,929
IVY: Hmm. Where did the extra ten go?

12
00:00:43,329 --> 00:00:46,095
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

13
00:00:46,495 --> 00:00:50,118
BRAMBLE: Can you point to the one-dollar coins?

14
00:00:53,718 --> 00:00:56,727
BRAMBLE: How much should be in the till?

15
00:00:57,127 --> 00:00:59,363
A. 55 dollars.

16
00:00:59,563 --> 00:01:02,055
B. 65 dollars.

17
00:01:02,255 --> 00:01:04,167
Pause and think.

18
00:01:08,767 --> 00:01:13,216
Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

19
00:01:13,616 --> 00:01:17,928
Eight coins and seven coins make fifteen coins.

20
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:22,550
Swap ten coins for one ten-dollar note.

21
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:27,327
Now there are six tens and five ones.

22
00:01:27,727 --> 00:01:29,973
That's 65 dollars.

23
00:01:30,373 --> 00:01:32,839
It's B! 65 dollars.

24
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:36,672
OTTO: Oh! I forgot the ten from the swap!

25
00:01:37,072 --> 00:01:41,041
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way. Take the sales away.

26
00:01:41,441 --> 00:01:47,806
65 take away 27. Five ones can't lose seven.

27
00:01:48,206 --> 00:01:52,507
So swap one ten for ten ones. Fifteen ones.

28
00:01:52,907 --> 00:01:55,944
Fifteen take away seven leaves eight.

29
00:01:56,344 --> 00:02:00,309
Five tens take away two tens leaves three.

30
00:02:00,709 --> 00:02:04,734
38 dollars. Just what the till started with!

31
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:07,225
IVY: Now the till balances!

32
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:08,933
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

33
00:02:10,433 --> 00:02:13,178
OTTO: Don't worry. I'll carry the ten!

34
00:02:13,578 --> 00:02:16,058
IVY: Not like a surfboard, Otto!

35
00:02:16,658 --> 00:02:21,447
Remember. Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

36
00:02:21,947 --> 00:02:28,180
Say it with me. Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

37
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:35,308
Try it at home. Bundle ten pegs to make one ten.

38
00:02:35,808 --> 00:02:39,639
Next case: ladybird dots at a glance.

